00:01:03.100 --> 00:01:04.915
- You heard the man, spin that wheel.

00:01:04.915 --> 00:01:07.748
(cosmic spinning)

00:01:09.870 --> 00:01:12.910
- [Chuck] Michael Gordon wants
to know will our sun go nova?

00:01:12.910 --> 00:01:14.750
- Or supernova?

00:01:14.750 --> 00:01:16.754
- Asking for a friend (laughs).

00:01:16.754 --> 00:01:17.780
(Neil laughs)

00:01:17.780 --> 00:01:18.830
- You lying (laughs).

00:01:21.860 --> 00:01:24.580
The sun will do neither.

00:01:24.580 --> 00:01:25.640
Neither.

00:01:25.640 --> 00:01:29.210
The sun is not that kind of star.

00:01:29.210 --> 00:01:32.300
The sun, as it gets older

00:01:32.300 --> 00:01:33.820
and wiser,

00:01:33.820 --> 00:01:36.560
it will ultimately exhaust
the fuel in its core and

00:01:36.560 --> 00:01:39.510
one of the things that goes on inside

00:01:39.510 --> 00:01:41.300
is that it begins

00:01:41.300 --> 00:01:43.430
sort of converting hydrogen into helium

00:01:43.430 --> 00:01:45.910
in an outer shell that works it's way,

00:01:45.910 --> 00:01:47.410
it's no longer doing it in the core,

00:01:47.410 --> 00:01:50.020
it's this shell that works it's way out.

00:01:50.020 --> 00:01:52.570
And, while it's doing
that, the sun will bloat

00:01:52.570 --> 00:01:54.640
and get huge and

00:01:54.640 --> 00:01:56.990
it will engulf the orbit of Mercury,

00:01:56.990 --> 00:02:01.180
then Venus, then it will
render Earth's oceans a boil.

00:02:01.180 --> 00:02:03.640
They will then evaporate
into the atmosphere,

00:02:03.640 --> 00:02:06.380
Earth's atmosphere will
evaporate into space

00:02:06.380 --> 00:02:09.150
as we lose our orbital stability

00:02:09.150 --> 00:02:12.180
and descend into the stellar abyss,

00:02:12.180 --> 00:02:15.559
vaporizing along the way.

00:02:15.559 --> 00:02:17.310
Have a nice day.

00:02:17.310 --> 00:02:20.296
- Wow Neil, you should really
write children's books.

00:02:20.296 --> 00:02:21.150
(Neil laughs)

00:02:21.150 --> 00:02:22.270
- There you go Michael,
I hope you're happy

00:02:22.270 --> 00:02:23.600
you killed us all.

00:02:23.600 --> 00:02:25.010
All right Neil, you ready
for another question?

00:02:25.010 --> 00:02:25.956
- Spin that wheel.

00:02:25.956 --> 00:02:28.789
(cosmic spinning)

00:02:29.760 --> 00:02:31.970
- [Chuck] Here we go,
Dorothy Wiseman wants to know

00:02:31.970 --> 00:02:35.070
how big of an asteroid would it take

00:02:35.070 --> 00:02:38.160
to totally destroy the Earth?

00:02:38.160 --> 00:02:39.820
- Sometimes when people say destroy Earth,

00:02:39.820 --> 00:02:41.480
they mean destroy life on Earth

00:02:41.480 --> 00:02:45.000
and all that takes is
asteroid 10 miles across

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:48.290
that'll do it because you
don't have to kill everybody,

00:02:48.290 --> 00:02:50.980
well, yeah, you'll kill
anybody who is where you hit,

00:02:50.980 --> 00:02:52.840
all right, they're gone instantly,

00:02:52.840 --> 00:02:54.690
but then how about everybody else?

00:02:54.690 --> 00:02:58.270
Well, since we all eat off of one another,

00:02:58.270 --> 00:03:01.410
if you take out the base of the food chain

00:03:01.410 --> 00:03:03.100
because you've cloaked the Earth

00:03:03.100 --> 00:03:06.380
in darkness from this asteroid impact,

00:03:06.380 --> 00:03:09.500
then that takes out the plants.

00:03:09.500 --> 00:03:10.660
And if you take out the plants,

00:03:10.660 --> 00:03:12.440
you take out the animals
that eat the plants,

00:03:12.440 --> 00:03:13.273
then you take out the animals

00:03:13.273 --> 00:03:14.810
that eat the animals that eat the plants.

00:03:14.810 --> 00:03:16.730
And this is a wave of extinction

00:03:16.730 --> 00:03:19.150
that percolates across the tree of life.

00:03:19.150 --> 00:03:21.270
10 miles across would do it.

00:03:21.270 --> 00:03:22.490
The one that took out the dinosaurs

00:03:22.490 --> 00:03:25.620
was about the size of Mount
Everest, about six miles across.

00:03:25.620 --> 00:03:27.620
If you want to obliterate
the entire Earth,

00:03:27.620 --> 00:03:30.000
there is no such object
out there to do so.

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:30.833
- Cool!

00:03:30.833 --> 00:03:33.320
I mean not cool, that's not cool.

00:03:33.320 --> 00:03:35.330
Will it make a difference
where that 10 mile asteroid

00:03:35.330 --> 00:03:36.460
will hit?

00:03:36.460 --> 00:03:39.170
- It won't make any difference at all.

00:03:39.170 --> 00:03:40.490
We're talking about how much energy

00:03:40.490 --> 00:03:42.720
is being plunked down onto Earth's surface

00:03:42.720 --> 00:03:44.910
and it's an energy
calculation at that point.

00:03:44.910 --> 00:03:48.510
Doesn't matter if it hits
land or ocean, doesn't matter.

00:03:48.510 --> 00:03:50.170
We think that something hits the ocean,

00:03:50.170 --> 00:03:52.010
the way we normally want to think about it

00:03:52.010 --> 00:03:54.193
is there's a tsunami
and the tsunami's bad.

00:03:56.820 --> 00:03:59.327
If your 10 miles across,

00:04:01.560 --> 00:04:03.550
you are bigger than the depth

00:04:03.550 --> 00:04:05.450
of most of the world's ocean,

00:04:05.450 --> 00:04:08.600
so the ocean just doesn't even matter.

00:04:08.600 --> 00:04:10.500
You're making a crater in
the bottom of the ocean

00:04:10.500 --> 00:04:14.280
when you hit, so no,
it just doesn't matter.

00:04:14.280 --> 00:04:15.660
Kiss your ass goodbye.

00:04:15.660 --> 00:04:17.100
- You know what I love about this episode?

00:04:17.100 --> 00:04:20.520
It's so uplifting, which is
why we're gonna take a break

00:04:20.520 --> 00:04:22.320
while I contemplate my own death.

00:04:22.320 --> 00:04:23.220
We'll be right back.

00:04:23.220 --> 00:04:24.053
(cosmic spinning)

